  "random_control_mechanism_derived": true,
  "random_control_mechanism_formula": "For directed random k-out graph, B_SP(i,1)={i}+N_i. For edge i->j, B_SP(i,1)\u2229B_SP(j,1) always contains j. It equals 1 iff N_j avoids the k forbidden vertices {i}\u222a(N_i\\{j}), with exact probability prod_{r=0}^{k-1}(n-1-k-r)/(n-1-r). L_CAP uses the min over k out-edges, so P(min intersection=1)\u22481-(1-p)^k. Thus random k-out has L_CAP\u22481/(k+1), making E_CAP rise with k and producing large k-spread.",
